From 26a99af657a898821a3557063a7def70fda53424 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?John=20T=C3=B6rnblom?= <john.tornblom@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 22:14:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] egl: add the videoout platform

-Dplatforms=videoout is EGL on the PS4's display, through zink on RADV
presenting with VK_KHR_display. It needs neither DRM nor a window
system: the display is the only window, and pbuffers are zink's own
images.

PS4 modules can't use each other's TLS variables, so the current
dispatch and context are read through calls, as on Windows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
